  "notes": "The Communion of the faithful: the showing of the Host, the priest's threefold Dómine non sum dignus, said facing those about to receive, and the form said to each of them. The three repetitions are encoded as three sets of words with their own ids, as at ordinarium.panem-caelestem and in the Kyrie. The one word that separates the two forms is TUAM at w067, where the priest's own form has meam. ECCE at w001 and w004 is tagged intj; Whitaker's heads it so, Collatinus carries it with no features at all, and the corpus's recorded classification ruling lets an analyzer call an interjection an adverb without counting as a divergence. The rubric at s01 prints ad communicandos as one word in witness do; the corpus sets the space, which the 1962 typical edition prints. This text's witnesses carry the Confiteor and absolution said before it as well; the Confiteor is already the corpus's ordinarium.confiteor, but the absolution is the rail's own form — peccatórum vestrórum, vobis, where ordinarium.misereatur has nostrórum, nobis — and that form the corpus does not yet carry.",
